The Protenix "protenix-v2" checkpoint is not currently served by its official
endpoint (which returns HTTP 403 for public requests). When the checkpoint is
absent, the pipeline downloads it at runtime from a third-party mirror
(huggingface.co/TMF001/pxdesign-weights) and verifies it against a pinned
SHA-256 before loading. That mirror is not affiliated with the Protenix
authors; the SHA-256 check ensures the fetched file is byte-identical to the
known-good checkpoint and refuses to load anything else. Protenix's code and
model parameters are both released under the Apache License 2.0 (per the
Protenix README), so redistribution of the checkpoint is permitted; users may
substitute an official copy where one is available.

